{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>They journeyed from here, for I heard, etc.</b> One needs to know for what purpose it was necessary to say <b>they journeyed from here</b>, and it would not have sufficed to say ״I heard them say, let us go״ etc.? And our Sages of blessed memory (Genesis Rabbah 84) interpreted that he told him they had journeyed from the pasture and gone to seek pretexts with which to kill him. And according to their words it is difficult: why was Yosef not startled to turn back, for there is no more obvious danger than this, and heaven forbid he would have been as one obligated in his own soul to endanger himself." "Or perhaps it is because Yosef did not understand the man's words as our Sages of blessed memory explained them. And our Sages of blessed memory explained it thus only after what the brothers did was revealed, whereas Yosef understood the things according to their plain sense in this manner: <b>they journeyed from here</b> — meaning, from that entire region, and he had no need to search further in that region, and the reason is <b>for I heard them say, let us go.</b> And from this he knew that they had uprooted their dwelling from that entire place, and he could not say ״they went to Dothan״ because he did not know clearly that they had gone to Dothan except from their words, and he recounted the order of events. And because it was in Yosef's mind that this man was a wayfarer and not an angel of HaShem, he understood the things according to their plain sense. And according to this, what the verse says — <b>Yosef went after his brothers and found them in Dothan</b> — is well understood, for it should have said ״Yosef went after his brothers to Dothan and found them.״ And according to what I have explained it comes out correctly: the angel did not affirm for him that they had gone to Dothan, only that they had journeyed from that place; therefore he searched for them by way of other places <b>and found them in Dothan</b>. Understand this. And the interpretation of our Sages stands in its place, for the Torah informed us that the angel spoke to him and hinted at the hidden matter." "It further intends its saying <b>after his brothers</b> — meaning, that Yosef interpreted the words of the speaker according to the interpretation of our Sages of blessed memory, and also understood the things according to their plain sense, and he weighed the interpretation that his intention was not to tell him they had journeyed from the pasture, but rather that they were still his brothers and friends; and this is its saying <b>after his brothers</b> — meaning, after establishing them in the status of brothers. And he interpreted the words of the speaker according to their plain sense as I explained above." "And if you say, if so, what did the angel accomplish with this information, since Yosef was not saved? Or perhaps it is that the intention was to multiply his reward when he would go after the pasture, as indeed he did. And with this too it will not be difficult how the angel could cause the nullification of what HaShem intended to do — to bring Yosef down to Egypt for great and wondrous reasons. Rather, he knew that his words would not nullify the matter, but rather they contain an enhancement of Yosef's merit. Or perhaps it is that through the agency of this matter HaShem completed for him a great measure and glory which he afterward attained in Egypt."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:46:42.496800338Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}